{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1178778-bloodlines-through-the-eras","id":1178778,"title":"Bloodlines Through the Eras","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-24T07:33:47-08:00","id":1178778,"title":"Bloodlines Through the Eras","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">With Dark Eras 2 coming eventually, Vampire now has quite a few Eras for us to play with (not enough for me, obviously ;D). I\u2019m already running two historical games, a Play-by-post Elizabethan game and my former Rome game that now is in Constantinople going from the Early Middle Ages to the High Middle Ages. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">So I\u2019ve decided to organize all the Bloodlines from the books by the time and location of it\u2019s \u201cbirth\u201d. Granted, some are harder to pinpoint, and there\u2019s nothing to say that their origin is just myth. I\u2019ve let players use \u201cfuture\u201d bloodlines like their it\u2019s actual founder. But I think it\u2019s an useful resource, and at least serves as inspiration for characters and groups for the storyteller to use. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">First I\u2019m going to list, and then do an Era by Era of which bloodlines I think can fit just fine.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>THE ANCIENT ONES</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">(These are the ones that are harder to pinpoint)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Noctuku (Bloodlines: The Chosen) - Very ancient, some believe neolithic.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- En (Ancient Bloodlines) - 12 thousand years. Sure.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Vedma (Ordo Dracul) - Claim to be older then the clans. Mostly in slavic lands.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Children of the Morrigan (Circle of the Crone) - 3000 years. Dwindled around the middle ages.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Kuufukuji (Bloodlines: The Legendary) - Ancient Asia. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Moroi (Ordo Dracul) - Seem very old. Romanian.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Adroanzi (Ancient Bloodlines) - Long before western civilization had knowledge of the African Continent.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Galloi (Bloodlines: The Legendary) - Claim to be 8000 years old. But believed to be during the Renaissance. Or even roman times.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Usiri (Ancient Bloodlines) - Ancient Egypt.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Bak-Ra (Ancient Bloodlines) - Ancient Egypt.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Khaibit (Bloodlines the Hidden) - Egypt at the time of Akhenaten. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Amara Havana (Ancient Bloodlines) - Ancient India.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Mayarap (Ancient Bloodlines) - Ancient Thailand.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Annunaku (Invictus) - Mesopotamia, probably. Spread during the Roman Empire.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Qedeshah (Bloodlines the Hidden) - Ancient Babylonia.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Iltani (Ancient Bloodlines)- Ancient Mesopotamia.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Rakshasa (Bloodlines the Hidden) - At least 500 B.C. India.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>ANCIENT GREECE</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Gorgons (Circle of the Crone) - Before the Camarilla, in greek lands. Waned during the times of Rome. Reappeared again in Constantinople after the fall of the Camarilla, but by the time of the Renaissance, disappeared again. Only to come back by the 19th century.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Agonistes (Bloodlines: The Chosen) - Ancient Greece.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Mnemosyne (Mekhet) - No one remembers, but they were there in Rome.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Hound\u2019s of Actdeon (Gangrel) - They believe they\u2019re ancient greek.<br /> - Kerberos (Onyx Path Homepage) - Two thousand years ago, in the greek isles.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>ROMAN TIMES</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Lygos (Nosferatu) - A child of Longinus, in Egypt. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Mortifiers of Flesh (Lancea Sanctum) - Origin lost, but at least as old as the Black Abbey (which is 335, supposedly).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Osites (Lancea Sanctum) - Origin lost. Supposedly one of the first Sanctified.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Alucinor (Bloodlines the Hidden) - Founded during the Roman Empire.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Morbus (Core Rules) - Since Ancient Roman Times.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Macellarius (Bloodlines: The Legendary) - Ancient Rome.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Larvae (Rome) - Ancient Rome. Not known if they still exist, but probably not.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Licini (Rome) - Ancient Rome.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Malocusians (Invictus) - Nothing about it\u2019s origins. But name of Discipline is based on roman architecture. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Special Snowflake:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Bron (Bloodlines: The Legendary) - Between 50 and 75 AD, or 500 B.C. in Britannia. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>EARLY MIDDLE AGES</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Baddacelli (Bloodlines: The Chosen) - Italy, after the fall of the Camarilla.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Canda Bhanu (Ancient Bloodlines) - India, after the fall of Roman Empire.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Anvari (Bloodlines the Hidden) - 4th or 5th Century, in Ancient Baghdad.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Taifa (Bloodlines: The Chosen) - Muslim Spain, 720s.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Yagnatia (Bloodlines: The Chosen) - 10th century Eastern Europe.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Norvegi (Mekhet) - North of Europe, during the Middle Ages.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Mystikoi (Ancient Bloodlines) - Constantinople, 976.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Spina (Invictus) - Founder Artus Le Jumel also founded the Most Honorable Order of the Thorned Wreath in 9th century France. Dead in 1350.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>HIGH MIDDLE AGES</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- The Mara (Circle of the Crone) - Origins seems celtic, Saxon and germanic. But earlier record is in the 11th century.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Order of Sir Martin (Ancient Bloodlines) - 11th Century, in the Holy Land.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Kallisti (Invictus) - Origin lost. A 1000 years ago, somewhere along the northernmost edge of Europe or Eastern Europe.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Rotgrafen (Bloodlines: The Chosen) - 1000 years ago, Norway.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Kinnaree (Ancient Bloodlines) - A Thousand years ago, in Thailand.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Nelapsi (Bloodlines the Hidden)- 12th Century, Czechoslovakia.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Corajoso (Ancient Bloodlines)- 13th century Portugal.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Icarians (Lancea Sanctum) - Founder Icarius, Archbishop of Naples, died in 1388.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Children of Judas (Bloodlines: The Legendary) - Maybe Serbia, 13th or 14th century.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Gullikan (Bloodlines: The Legendary) - 14th century Constantinople. </span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>15th CENTURY</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Asn\u00e2m (Circle of the Crone) - Founded by Atiqua Azad, and arab slaver in the late 1400\u2019s.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Tismanu (Ordo Dracul) - Wallachia, older then dracula (but not much, and unlike the Moroi seem to be), but only spread after him.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Azerkatil (Ordo Dracul) - 15th century Ottoman Empire</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>16th CENTURY</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Gethsemani (Bloodlines the Hidden) - 1522 Florence.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Morotrophians (Bloodlines the Hidden) - 16th Century Italy.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Sangiovanni (Bloodlines: The Chosen) - Venetia, during the Renaissance. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Geheim (Ancient Bloodlines) - 1577, Vienna and Switizerland.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>17th CENTURY</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Erzsebet (Daeva) - 17th Century Italy.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Architects of the Monolith (Bloodlines the Hidden)- 17th Century Paris.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Burakumin (Core Rules) - Feudal japan.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Sotoha (Invictus) - Founder was embraced at the beginning of 16th century japan. Left for America in the 17th century.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Septemi (Ancient Bloodlines) - Ostensible founder embraced during the Hundred Years War, in France. But bloodline might be older.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>18th CENTURY</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Toreador (Core Rules) - Spain during King Philip V\u2019s reign (1700-1724)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- The Carnival (Bloodlines: The Legendary) - 18th Century Bohemia.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Mellisidae (Bloodlines: The Legendary)- 18th century Britain.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Duchagne (Bloodlines: The Chosen) - 1765 France</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Tianpan Xiao (Bloodlines: The Chosen)- China, height of Qing Dynasty.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Apollinaire (Ancient Bloodlines) - Haiti, 1791.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Les Gens Libres (Ancient Bloodlines) - Haiti, 1791.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>19th CENTURY</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Nahualli (Bloodlines the Hidden) - 19th Century Mexico.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Oberlochs (Bloodlines the Hidden) - 19th Century, Pennsylvania.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Bohagande (Bloodlines the Hidden) - 1850s, Mojave desert.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Barjot (Carthians) - 1860\u2019s France.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Malkovians (Core Rules) - Between 1864 (Broadmoor Hospital\u2019s first male patients) - 1889 (Malkov\u2019s death)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Californai Xiao (Bloodlines: The Chosen) - 19th century California.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Sta-Au (Ancient Bloodlines) - 1800s America.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Shepperds (Ancient Bloodlines) - 19th century with the Montrose Party.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Mabry (Gangrel) - 1800\u2019s Alaska.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- The Cockscomb Society (Nosferatu) - 19th century England (tied to the Blackwood Abbey).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Dragolescu (Ordo Dracul) - Founder arrived in London in 1884, Bloodline seems to have started in 1901.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Libitinarius (Ordo Dracul) - Cult began in 1880\u2019s College of London. Bloodline began around 1892-1911.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>20th CENTURY</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Caporetti (Ancient Bloodlines) - Battle of Caporetto, 1917</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Brothers of Ypres (Ancient Bloodlines)- Battle of Ypres, 1915.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Players (Bloodlines: The Legendary)- 60 to 80 years ago in Hollywood.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Bruja (Core Rules) - 1940\u2019s American Southwest.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Carnon (Circle of the Crone) - San Francisco in the 1960\u2019s.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Deucalion (Carthians) - Last 50 years, New York.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Adrestoi (Ventrue) - 1980\u2019s Detroit.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Zelani (Carthians) - Hard to pin Lorna Zelani\u2019s embrace. But she woke 10 years ago (from 2006) and began spreading her blood. No source of where, but I guess it\u2019s your game\u2019s city. It sure is mine. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>21st CENTURY</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Lynx (Invictus) - Months ago as of the Invictus book release, which was in 2005.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>THE DARK ERAS AND THEIR BLOODLINES</b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>REQUIEM FOR ROME</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Obviously, everything from ROMAN TIMES and before is game. Just take notice of all those Lancea Sanctum bloodlines, that might or might not exist in your game still, depending the year. Also, the Bron would only be relevant in a Britannia setting, instead of the regular Rome one. I think the Greek and Babylonian bloodlines would work fine, as the Noctuku, Children of Morrigan and the Galloi, if you want them.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>THE SOULLESS AND THE DEAD (1346 - 1353)</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Now we\u2019re the in High Middle Ages, up to the 14th century. The setting has two scenarios for Vampires: Constantinople and Florence.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">A lot of those Bloodlines fit with Constantinople, specially (in my opinion): The Mara, kallisti, Rotgrafen (It\u2019s the time of their first incursions), Children of Judas, Taifa, Norvegi. The Gullikan, Mistikoi and Agonistes are very strong in Constantinople. The Gorgons too, but they are starting to fade here. The Bloodlines of Ancient Greece might be strong here as well. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">In Florence, we have the bloodlines that appear around it: Icarians, Baddacelli, as the Roman ones that might still be strong, like the Macellarius. Perhaps those from other parts of Europe, like the Carajoso, Spina and Norvegi.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>REQUIEM FOR REGINA (1590s)</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Not much to add from Florence, except those two centuries :P</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The bloodlines of the 15th century fit very little, but obviously it depends of the stories you\u2019re telling and the Asnam could be fun. The Morothropians can work lovely with Bedlam and the Rotgrafen are active again.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>DARK ERAS 2</b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>KING ARTHUR\u2019S BRITANNIA </b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Now we\u2019re going back to the Early Middle Ages. The Bron seems to fit this setting perfectly. I Imagine the Children of the Morrigan would have a lot of influence in this setting as well. And I can see the Mara being already active in this Era.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Another thing. With the setting being a crossover with Changeling, what about the Bugman from Immortal Sinners? He seems to be from a lost bloodline, which is very akin to the old Kyasid from Masquerade. Hopefully we see something in this Era. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>FRENCH REVOLUTION</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Duchagne could be fun during this Era. We see the rise of a lot of cool Bloodlines around Europe, like the Mellisidae and the Architects of the Monolith. The Septemi are active here and their supposed origin is in France. And maybe the Spina are strong around here. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I\u2019ll refrain from the Islamic Golden Age because I don\u2019t know much about the setting, but I\u2019m sure someone can give us their take. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">So thoughts? I know I made some mistakes, as well. How do you guys fit those bloodlines in your eras?</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":196,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","user":"Max Deltree","date":". 01-24-2018, 01:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T09:12:24-08:00","id":1178821,"title":"","content":